    "show_share": true,
    "description": "On-the-job training is regarded as one of the most effective ways to curb skill gaps at the workplace. However, this requires employers to invest monetary and non-monetary resources into training sessions and mentorship programmes. The repurcussions of under-prepared employees in the workplace reinforces the need for on-the-job training.",
